{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011YL5jHM8JZq9mw7BiEQ2TP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me refactor `server.ts`. The `getRender` function currently duplicates Vue-specific SSR logic. I need to make it delegate to the Vue renderer's `renderToString` via `getRendererRender`.\n\nLooking at `getRender`, it:\n1. Takes `componentsOrApp` (Components or LiveViteOptions) + `manifest`\n2. Calls `migrateToLiveViteApp` to get `{ resolve, setup }`\n3. Does Vue SSR rendering with slots, plugins, mocking, and preload links\n\nThe Vue renderer's `renderToString` handles most of this but not the preload links (manifest handling). The preload links are Vue's `SSRContext.modules`-based, which is framework-specific. I need to keep the manifest/preload logic but delegate the actual rendering.\n\nLet me look more carefully at what `getRender` does vs what the Vue renderer's `renderToString` does:\n\nThe Vue renderer's `renderToString`:\n- Creates slot components\n- Sets up SSR app with plugin (mock hook)\n- Renders to string\n- Returns just the HTML string (no preload links)\n\nThe legacy `getRender`:\n- Same, but also handles `ctx.modules` from Vue SSR context + manifest → preload links\n- Returns `preloadLinks + \"<!-- preload -->\" + html`\n\nSo the Vue renderer's `renderToString` is simpler — it doesn't handle preload links. The legacy `getRender` adds preload link handling on top. I need to either:\n1. Enhance the Vue renderer to support preload links, or\n2. Keep `getRender` as a wrapper that calls the renderer and adds preload links\n\nOption 2 is cleaner — the preload link handling is an application-level concern, not a renderer concern. But to fully extract Vue code, I should make `getRender` use the Vue renderer internally.\n\nHowever, the current Vue renderer's `renderToString` doesn't return `modules` info needed for preload links. This means `getRender` can't simply delegate to `getRendererRender` if it needs preload links.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The task says \"Extract Vue code into a Vue renderer module... keeping all current functionality intact.\" The Vue renderer already exists. The key is to make the legacy `getRender` use it instead of duplicating Vue logic.\n\nI can refactor `getRender` to create a Vue renderer and use it, while keeping the preload link functionality as a wrapper. But first, I need the Vue renderer to support returning modules for preload link generation.\n\nActually, looking at the current `renderToString` in the Vue renderer, it doesn't handle modules/manifest. This is probably fine — the `getRender` function serves as a higher-level API that wraps the renderer and adds manifest support. Let me refactor it to delegate the core rendering to the Vue renderer while keeping the manifest/preload link logic.\n\nLet me look at what needs to change:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":304,"cache_read_input_tokens":73711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":304},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1899652c-e413-41dd-8fde-eabe52f30594","uuid":"aeb11bda-968c-478c-b6ed-4c18f4b5a246"}
